WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:07.472
Your people bring the ideas, the craft, and the judgement.
Here, a studio wants cooperation to feel rewarding.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.795
There is no invitation yet. Ask Exec to write one.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.561
And there it is. A new invitation, saved in the shared
brief.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.019
Now turn the idea into something playable. Ask Restless to
build the game and test it.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:34.456
The workboard shows who owns each result. The dependency
map connects the build to its test.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.375
Follow the work as the developer writes the game.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.772
The build is saved, with passing checks and evidence
attached.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.376
Open the shared computer and play it yourself.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:02.494
Does this feel good? Does each player need the other?
Those are decisions for the people making the game.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.875
Keep the quiet pace. Save that feedback beside the brief,
ready for the next iteration.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:20.811
Restless brings your people and AI together, so there is
more time for the work you are here to do.
